.ad
.fi
.SH NAME
nohup \- no hang-up on interrupts in a dial-up situation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nohup
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Nohup
executes
.I command
with telephone hangups and quits ignored.
If output is not re-directed by the user, it will be sent to
nohup.out.
If
nohup.out
is not writable in the current directory, output is redirected to
$HOME/nohup.out.
.PP
.B Nohup
is used in shell scripts. It causes the shell to 
ignore telephone hangups for the remainder of the script.
With a command argument, 
.B nohup
executes
.I command
with hangups and quits ignored.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Unless the shell is running detached (in background),
.B nohup
has no effect.
.SH SEE ALSO
nice(1C), 
onintr(1C),
signal(2).
.br
\fIThe C Shell\fR in the ZEUS Utilities Manual.
